    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "Thus, the phenotypic correlation between two traits is entirely described in terms of correlations between components of the traits and their heritabilities. Frequently in quantitative-genetic applications, the correlations between $ E_x $ and $ G_y $ and between $ E_y $ and $ G_x $ are zero. In this case, Equation A2.12 reduces to",
